title: Washington Wants One Polish Answer
subtitle: The White House, Congress, defence and the Palace are different relationships.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_foreign_card
frequency: 95
view-if: month_actions < max_month_actions and us_election_2020_done = 1 and poland_white_house_pressure_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_white_house_pressure_timer = 6; foreign_cards_resolved += 1; foreign_pressure += 2
card-image: img/poland/cards/presidential-channel.webp

= Washington wants one Polish answer

**President:** [+ us_president +] · **administration:** [+
us_administration +]  
Alliance reliability **[+ us_alliance_reliability +]** · ambassador **[+
us_ambassador_channel +]** · Congress **[+ us_congress_channel +]** · defence
**[+ us_defence_channel +]**

[? if us_administration = "Democratic": Washington links NATO coordination to
democratic institutions, Ukraine and a common European line. PiS calls the
package partisan pressure; KO wants to own the relationship.?]
[? if us_administration != "Democratic": Washington asks for spending,
bilateral loyalty and visible alignment while treating EU coordination as a
competitor. PiS claims a privileged channel; the Left's Atlanticists fear an
avoidable rupture.?]

- @institutions
- @bilateral
