@institutions
title: Diversify through Congress, defence officials and parliamentary committees
subtitle: Congress +6, defence +3 and reliability +3.
on-arrival: us_congress_channel += 6; us_defence_channel += 3; us_ambassador_channel += 2; us_alliance_reliability += 3; constitutional_restraint += 2; public_trust += 2; foreign_pressure -= 2; news_headline = "The American relationship becomes larger than one president"

A later election can reverse the White House without erasing every working
contact. The investment is deliberately unglamorous.

- #poland_card_finish

@bilateral
title: Give the administration the visible bilateral pledge it wants
subtitle: Defence +6 and Palace relations +4; EU influence −3 and party unity −2.
on-arrival: us_defence_channel += 6; us_ambassador_channel += 5; president_relation += 4; pis_relation += 3 if us_administration != "Democratic"; ko_relation += 2 if us_administration = "Democratic"; eu_influence -= 3; party_unity -= 2; left_atlanticist_dissent -= 3; foreign_pressure -= 3; news_headline = "A bilateral pledge restores access and narrows Poland's room"

The meeting produces an assurance and a photograph. European partners and
Left critics both ask which concession was omitted from the communiqué.

- #poland_card_finish

@european
title: Build a European pillar before answering Washington
subtitle: EU influence +5 and eastern coalition +4; US defence −2 and Atlanticist dissent +4.
on-arrival: eu_influence += 5; eu_eastern_coalition += 4; france_relation += 2; germany_relation += 2; us_ambassador_channel -= 2; us_defence_channel -= 2; left_atlanticist_dissent += 4; foreign_pressure += 1; news_headline = "Warsaw answers Washington through a stronger European pillar"

Strategic autonomy becomes a negotiating position rather than an exit from
NATO. The distinction is clear in the document and much less clear on Polish
television.

- #poland_card_finish
